                Monsters in Molasses

I've been standing by an altar to Kos, deity of my
now XL 9 AC 0 rogue, searching until something shows
up to kill.  My XL is now high enough to create
yellow lights, and has been high enough for floating
eyes for quite a while.

So, I'd long ago achieved mental acuity, and even
though I nailed the oncoming yellow light with some
daggers, I got blinded.

Which means I can see all non-mindless monsters on
the level. Unfortunately, it is the ascii version
of the graphic nethack, so I can't cut and paste it,
but I can count it for you. There are 118 monsters
somewhere on DLVL 1, not counting my PC. Mostly,
they are stuck, behind sleeping nymphs, leprachauns,
or nearly immobile piercers or slow moving floating
eyes.

Sacrificing keeps paying dividends, I just got
Dragonsbane to add to Sting and Stormbringer, though
they're going to have to wrest Stormy from my cold,
dead fingers; this artifact *rocks*.

It is going to be tough convincing myself not to go
wandering off for nourishment and mischief, but
after 41,500 turns all on DLVL 1, I suspect I have a
working plan in action; I've long ago had to drop
my sack, the death dropped goodies in it are getting
heavy, and the pile of crud in the corner is now a
couple of screens high when listed.

I suspect over time that rockmoles and dwarves will
carve all the communicating passages needed to
unblock the way for the ravening hordes waiting to
attack my PC. Sadly, that will include side doors
through which nymphs can sneak close before
attacking. I can only hope some cooperative monster
drops an uncursed blindfold or towel soon. I'd better
put a backup stash of daggers in my sack for nymph
pursuit, too.

xanthian.

I have a wand of polymorph now, resisting the urge
to use it at least until I have something worth
polymorphing will be tough. I suppose once I'm seeing
golems anyway, zapping the pile of crud might be worth
the effort.


